This paper examines a specific system of partial differential equations:
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
-\Delta u + |v|^{p-1}v = 0, \\
-\Delta v + |u|^{q-1}v = 0,
\end{cases}
\quad u, v \in H^1(\mathbb{R}^N),
\end{equation}
where $N \geq 3$. The exponents $p$ and $q$ are constrained by $p>1$, $q>1$, and the condition $2<p+q<\frac{N+2}{N-1}$. The study establishes the existence of positive solutions for this system.
